# rfc-005-document-system.mdc

## Title
RFC 005 – Markdown Document System (Notion-like)

## Summary
This RFC defines the structure and integration of a document system for course-related content. It enables course creators to include markdown-based documents for richer educational materials.

---

## Goals
- Create markdown-based documents using WYSIWYG editor (TipTap)
- Allow documents to be linked to courses or made globally available
- Render documents with rich formatting (headings, code blocks, lists, etc.)
- (Phase 2) Enable user note-taking or commenting

## Database Tables
### `documents`
| Field         | Type      | Description                         |
|---------------|-----------|-------------------------------------|
| id            | uuid      | Primary key                         |
| title         | text      | Document title                      |
| slug          | text      | URL-friendly identifier             |
| content       | text      | Markdown or JSON-based document     |
| linked_course | uuid      | Nullable FK to `courses`            |
| is_global     | boolean   | If true, shown in general library   |
| created_by    | uuid      | Creator user ID                     |
| created_at    | timestamp | Created timestamp                   |

## Editor Component
- Use TipTap editor (customizable Notion-style experience)
- Support standard markdown blocks (headings, bold, italic, lists, code)
- Optional image and link embeds

## Viewer Component
- Render formatted document content
- Sidebar for in-page navigation (optional)

## Role Permissions
- Admin/Team Lead: Create, edit, delete documents
- User: View linked documents in courses, global docs
- Guest: (Optional Phase 2) View limited docs

## UI Locations
- Course Detail Page: If course has documents, show them in a tab
- Global Docs Library: Available to all roles (based on access level)

## Validation
- Title and content required
- Slug must be unique

## Timeline
**Sprint 5**
- Create `documents` table
- Integrate TipTap editor in admin/lead UI
- Implement document viewer and link to courses

